\ walletrun.fam — drives the wallet as wm does (docs/GUI_WALLET.md): runs
\ /bin/wallet on two pipes, writes it each line of /lib/wreq, and prints
\ each line it answers as "w: <line>" (one answer a request; wm's unlock
\ line the first of each run).  A line "---" ends that wallet (its input
\ closed, its end waited for) and starts another; "--- /dir" starts it
\ in /dir (made), so a fresh wallet there.  A test program, not
\ in the image: oscheck's wallet checks build it with the wallet.
: rq variable ;  : rqn variable ;  : pin variable ;  : pout variable ;  : fdv variable ;  : pid variable ;
: ab variable ;  : an variable ;  : lp variable ;  : st variable ;  : wargs variable ;
: wstart
pin @ pipe drop  pout @ pipe drop
3 lit fdv @ !  pin @ @ fdv @ 4 lit + !  pout @ 4 lit + @ fdv @ 8 lit + !  2 lit fdv @ C lit + !
"wallet" wargs @ fdv @ spawnv pid !
pin @ @ close drop  pout @ 4 lit + @ close drop  0 lit an ! ;
: wstop  pin @ 4 lit + @ close drop  pid @ st @ wait drop  pout @ @ close drop ;
\ wnl ( -- i )  where the first newline of what was read is (an: none).
: wnl  0 lit begin dup an @ u< if dup ab @ + c@ A lit <> else 0 lit then while 1 lit + repeat ;
\ wev ( -- flag )  the line at ab an event ({"ev...): unasked, not an
\ answer (the block thread's word that no node is reached comes when it
\ comes, docs/TIMING_FIXES.md item 15), so not taken for one.
: wev  ab @ c@ 7B lit =  ab @ 1 lit + c@ 22 lit = and  ab @ 2 lit + c@ 65 lit = and  ab @ 3 lit + c@ 76 lit = and ;
\ wline1 ( -- event? )  the wallet's next line, printed unless an event
\ ("(it ended)" if it ended first).
: wline1
begin wnl an @ = while
	pout @ @ ab @ an @ + FFF lit an @ - read
	dup 0 lit > if an @ + an ! else
		drop ab @ an @ + "(it ended)" scpy A lit over c! 1 lit + ab @ - an !
	then
repeat
wnl  0 lit over ab @ + c!  wev dup 0= if "w: " puts ab @ puts 0A lit putc then
swap
an @ over 1 lit + - ?dup if 0 lit do ab @ over 1 lit + + i + c@ ab @ i + c! loop then
an @ swap 1 lit + - an ! ;
\ wline  the wallet's next answer, printed (its events passed over).
: wline  begin wline1 0= until ;

: ls variable ;  : le variable ;  : nl variable ;
\ isdash ( a -- flag )  the line at a is "---".
: isdash
dup c@ 2D lit =  over 1 lit + c@ 2D lit = and  over 2 lit + c@ 2D lit = and
swap 3 lit + c@ dup A lit = over 0= or swap 20 lit = or and ;
1000 lit alloc rq !  1000 lit alloc ab !  8 lit alloc pin !  8 lit alloc pout !  10 lit alloc fdv !  8 lit alloc st !  4 lit alloc nl !
A lit nl @ c!  10 lit alloc wargs !  wargs @ "wallet" scpy 0 lit over c! 0 lit swap 1 lit + c!
"/lib/wreq" 0 lit open dup rq @ FFF lit read rqn ! close drop  0 lit rq @ rqn @ + c!
wstart
rq @ lp !
begin lp @ c@ while
	lp @ ls !  lp @ begin dup c@ dup A lit <> and while 1 lit + repeat le !
	ls @ isdash if
		wstop
		ls @ 3 lit + c@ 20 lit = if
			0 lit le @ c!  ls @ 4 lit + mkdir drop
			"/proc/self/cwd" 1 lit open dup ls @ 4 lit + dup strlen write drop close drop
			A lit le @ c!
		then
		wstart
	else
		pin @ 4 lit + @ ls @ le @ ls @ - write drop  pin @ 4 lit + @ nl @ 1 lit write drop
		wline
	then
	le @ c@ if le @ 1 lit + else le @ then lp !
repeat
wstop
"walletrun: done" puts 0A lit putc
0 lit exit
